# File: scripts/__tests__/coverage-report-v2.test.mjs
# Generated from: specs/615-read-per-test-coverage-reports-from-a-file-in-a-streamable-range-compressed-format-so-large-suites-do-not-overflow-the-256-mib-stdout-buffer/requirements.md
Feature: Read per-test coverage reports from a file in a streamable, range-compressed format

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: A v2 report larger than 256 MiB is read from the provided path
    Given a coverage command that writes a v2 report larger than 256 MiB to the path in NMG_SDLC_COVERAGE_OUTPUT
    When test-layers-candidates runs
    Then it records the baseline
    And it lists the migration batches

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario Outline: A v1 report on stdout keeps working unchanged
    Given a coverage command that prints a v1 report on stdout and writes no file
    When <consumer> runs
    Then its result equals the result for the same v1 report before this change

    Examples:
      | consumer                              |
      | test-layers-candidates                |
      | test-layers-batch begin               |
      | test-layers-batch gate                |
      | test-layers-report                    |
      | the verification gate coverage check  |

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario Outline: A malformed v2 line refuses with its line number
    Given a v2 report whose line <line> is <defect>
    When <consumer> reads it
    Then the run refuses with <reason>
    And the message names line <line>

    Examples:
      | line | defect                 | consumer                             | reason                     |
      | 3    | invalid JSON           | test-layers-candidates               | test_layers_coverage_failed |
      | 1    | missing the v2 header  | test-layers-candidates               | test_layers_coverage_failed |
      | 2    | a reversed range [5,2] | the verification gate coverage check | coverage_failed            |
      | 4    | a duplicate test id    | the verification gate coverage check | coverage_failed            |

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: v1 and v2 forms of the same coverage classify identically
    Given the same coverage written once as a v1 report and once as a v2 report
    When candidates and the batch gate run against each
    Then the duplicate and convert classification is identical
    And the accepted evidence and the coverage gap are identical

  @SCN005 @regression
  Scenario: Begin state round-trips without a suite-sized string
    Given a batch begun against a v2 report of at least 2000 tests
    When test-layers-batch gate accepts one batch and refuses another
    Then the begin state is stored one test per line
    And no single string built while storing or reading it exceeds 64 KiB
    And the gate decisions equal those of the equivalent v1 run

  @SCN006
  Scenario: The references describe the v2 contract
    Given the verification-scope, steering-schema and test-layer-migration references
    When they are read
    Then each names NMG_SDLC_COVERAGE_OUTPUT, the version 2 header, one test per line, line ranges, branch triples and the v1 stdout fallback
